1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,472
Ask who did not ride a
bicycle to college today.

2
00:00:03,472 --> 00:00:06,587
In your class, the answer
is a handful of names.

3
00:00:06,587 --> 00:00:09,023
In the whole college, it is hundreds.

4
00:00:09,423 --> 00:00:10,469
Same question.

5
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:12,013
Very different answers.

6
00:00:12,013 --> 00:00:14,279
It depends on who you count from.

7
00:00:14,729 --> 00:00:18,560
Aarav wondered about this as he
locked his bicycle this morning.

8
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:22,761
In his group of seven friends,
only three rode a bicycle.

9
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:23,998
So who did not?

10
00:00:24,498 --> 00:00:28,396
To answer, you need the riders,
and the full list you start from.

11
00:00:28,396 --> 00:00:30,415
That is the idea of a complement.

12
00:00:31,065 --> 00:00:33,234
First, recall the universal set.

13
00:00:33,234 --> 00:00:36,831
It is the full set we work
inside, and we call it U.

14
00:00:37,181 --> 00:00:39,240
Here, U is the seven friends.

15
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:43,168
A is the friends who rode a
bicycle: Aarav, Kiran and Ravi.

16
00:00:43,568 --> 00:00:47,781
The complement of A is the set of
all elements of U that are not in A.

17
00:00:47,781 --> 00:00:51,342
We write A with a small dash,
and read it as A complement.

18
00:00:51,742 --> 00:00:53,056
Watch the test run.

19
00:00:53,056 --> 00:00:56,498
Take each friend in U, and
ask: is this friend in A?

20
00:00:56,898 --> 00:00:57,798
Aarav?

21
00:00:57,448 --> 00:00:58,348
In A.

22
00:00:58,008 --> 00:00:58,908
Diya?

23
00:00:58,513 --> 00:01:01,121
Not in A, so she goes to the complement.

24
00:01:01,121 --> 00:01:02,021
Kiran?

25
00:01:01,672 --> 00:01:02,572
In A.

26
00:01:02,631 --> 00:01:06,701
Joel and Meera did not ride,
so they go to the complement.

27
00:01:06,701 --> 00:01:07,601
Ravi did.

28
00:01:07,542 --> 00:01:08,649
Sana did not.

29
00:01:09,049 --> 00:01:12,086
So A complement is Diya,
Joel, Meera and Sana.

30
00:01:12,086 --> 00:01:16,213
In the picture, it is everything
inside the rectangle, but outside the

31
00:01:16,213 --> 00:01:17,113
circle.

32
00:01:17,472 --> 00:01:22,595
In set builder form, A complement is
the set of all x, such that x is in

33
00:01:22,595 --> 00:01:24,509
U, and x is not in A.

34
00:01:25,259 --> 00:01:29,124
Now change the universal set,
and watch the complement change.

35
00:01:29,524 --> 00:01:33,161
Let A be the even numbers
two, four, six, eight and ten.

36
00:01:33,161 --> 00:01:36,021
First, take U as the
numbers from one to ten.

37
00:01:36,421 --> 00:01:38,768
A complement is the five odd numbers.

38
00:01:38,768 --> 00:01:41,153
One, three, five, seven and nine.

39
00:01:41,553 --> 00:01:44,558
Now let U grow, all the way up to twenty.

40
00:01:44,558 --> 00:01:46,362
A stays exactly the same.

41
00:01:46,762 --> 00:01:48,791
But A complement keeps growing.

42
00:01:48,791 --> 00:01:50,676
Now it has fifteen elements.

43
00:01:50,676 --> 00:01:52,957
The complement always depends on U.

44
00:01:53,607 --> 00:01:54,732
Side by side.

45
00:01:54,732 --> 00:01:57,533
A complement is the same as U minus A.

46
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:00,804
You start from everything
in U, and remove A.

47
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,427
B minus A starts only from B.

48
00:02:03,427 --> 00:02:08,482
With B as the numbers from one to
six, B minus A is just one, three and

49
00:02:08,482 --> 00:02:09,382
five.

50
00:02:09,669 --> 00:02:10,643
Now you try.

51
00:02:10,643 --> 00:02:14,852
U is the numbers from one to
ten, and A is one, two and three.

52
00:02:14,852 --> 00:02:17,425
How many elements does A complement have?

53
00:02:17,425 --> 00:02:18,635
Pause and decide.

54
00:02:21,835 --> 00:02:22,735
Seven!

55
00:02:22,421 --> 00:02:24,301
The numbers four up to ten.

56
00:02:24,301 --> 00:02:27,324
Ten elements in U, take
away the three in A.

57
00:02:27,974 --> 00:02:29,004
Remember this.

58
00:02:29,004 --> 00:02:32,335
The complement is everything
in U that is not in A.

59
00:02:33,035 --> 00:02:35,789
Now four laws follow,
straight from the picture.

60
00:02:36,139 --> 00:02:37,039
Step one.

61
00:02:37,039 --> 00:02:41,001
Every element of U is either
inside A, or outside A.

62
00:02:41,001 --> 00:02:43,328
So A union A complement is U.

63
00:02:44,078 --> 00:02:44,978
Step two.

64
00:02:44,925 --> 00:02:48,986
No element can be inside A and
outside A at the same time.

65
00:02:48,986 --> 00:02:52,283
So A intersection A
complement is the empty set.

66
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:53,933
Step three.

67
00:02:53,926 --> 00:02:55,664
Take the complement twice.

68
00:02:55,664 --> 00:02:58,411
The outside of the outside is back inside.

69
00:02:58,411 --> 00:03:01,013
So the complement of A complement is A.

70
00:03:01,763 --> 00:03:02,663
Step four.

71
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:06,956
Nothing in U lies outside U, so
U complement is the empty set.

72
00:03:06,956 --> 00:03:10,326
And the complement of the
empty set is all of U.

73
00:03:11,076 --> 00:03:11,976
Quick one.

74
00:03:11,898 --> 00:03:15,591
In Aarav's group, who is in
the complement of A complement?

75
00:03:15,591 --> 00:03:16,753
Pause and think.

76
00:03:19,953 --> 00:03:20,853
The riders!

77
00:03:20,843 --> 00:03:22,478
Aarav, Kiran and Ravi.

78
00:03:22,478 --> 00:03:25,612
Taking the complement
twice brings you back to A.

79
00:03:26,262 --> 00:03:27,997
Now, one worked example.

80
00:03:28,347 --> 00:03:31,098
U is the natural numbers from one to ten.

81
00:03:31,098 --> 00:03:33,558
A is the set of prime numbers in U.

82
00:03:33,558 --> 00:03:34,846
Find A complement.

83
00:03:35,346 --> 00:03:36,246
Step one.

84
00:03:36,139 --> 00:03:39,338
U is one, two, three, and so on up to ten.

85
00:03:39,338 --> 00:03:40,324
Ten elements.

86
00:03:41,074 --> 00:03:41,974
Step two.

87
00:03:41,828 --> 00:03:45,241
The primes up to ten are
two, three, five and seven.

88
00:03:45,991 --> 00:03:46,891
Step three.

89
00:03:46,886 --> 00:03:48,285
Remove them from U.

90
00:03:48,285 --> 00:03:52,027
A complement is one, four,
six, eight, nine and ten.

91
00:03:52,777 --> 00:03:53,677
Step four.

92
00:03:53,595 --> 00:03:54,495
Check.

93
00:03:54,168 --> 00:03:58,435
Four elements in A, plus six in
A complement, gives all ten in U.

94
00:03:59,185 --> 00:04:00,811
And notice the number one.

95
00:04:00,811 --> 00:04:03,894
One is not a prime, so it
belongs to A complement.

96
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:06,010
Now, the exam trap.

97
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,024
A is one, two and three.

98
00:04:08,024 --> 00:04:12,178
Many students write A complement as
every other number: four, five, six,

99
00:04:12,178 --> 00:04:13,206
and on forever.

100
00:04:13,606 --> 00:04:16,824
But a complement only makes
sense inside a given U.

101
00:04:16,824 --> 00:04:20,543
If U is one to five, A
complement is just four and five.

102
00:04:21,193 --> 00:04:22,763
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:26,946
In PUC board exams, as: find
A complement for a given U.

104
00:04:26,946 --> 00:04:30,951
And in JEE Main, often mixed
with intervals and integers.

105
00:04:31,551 --> 00:04:32,759
Exam level now.

106
00:04:32,759 --> 00:04:35,390
How many elements are in A complement?

107
00:04:35,390 --> 00:04:36,649
Pause and solve.

108
00:04:42,049 --> 00:04:43,377
The answer is A.

109
00:04:43,377 --> 00:04:44,427
Eighty eight.

110
00:04:44,927 --> 00:04:49,340
The perfect squares up to one hundred
are one, four, nine, and so on up

111
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,425
to one hundred.

112
00:04:50,425 --> 00:04:51,796
That is ten numbers.

113
00:04:52,296 --> 00:04:56,201
The perfect cubes are one, eight,
twenty seven and sixty four.

114
00:04:56,201 --> 00:05:00,311
One and sixty four are already
squares, so only eight and twenty seven

115
00:05:00,311 --> 00:05:01,211
are new.

116
00:05:01,525 --> 00:05:05,891
So A has twelve elements, and A
complement has one hundred minus twelve.

117
00:05:05,891 --> 00:05:07,313
That is eighty eight.

118
00:05:07,913 --> 00:05:09,373
Here is your recap.

119
00:05:09,373 --> 00:05:10,874
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:14,074 --> 00:05:16,911
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

121
00:05:17,311 --> 00:05:18,211
One.

122
00:05:17,829 --> 00:05:19,920
What is A union A complement?

123
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:21,720
Two.

124
00:05:21,286 --> 00:05:25,495
If U is one to six, and A is two
and four, what is A complement?

125
00:05:26,395 --> 00:05:27,295
Three.

126
00:05:26,983 --> 00:05:30,164
Why must you know U before
you find a complement?

127
00:05:31,264 --> 00:05:36,095
Next time: Diya sorts her classmates
into circles for Biology and Maths.

128
00:05:36,095 --> 00:05:37,316
Who goes where?

129
00:05:37,316 --> 00:05:39,499
We draw it with Venn diagrams.
